The `section()` method has an ugly double-negative condition. Let's clean this up:

```php
private static function section(array $data, string $name): array
{
    if (!\array_key_exists($name, $data) || $data[$name] === null) {
        return [];
    }
    $value = $data[$name];
    if (!\is_array($value) || !array_is_list($value)) {
        throw new ImportException(sprintf('The "%s" section must be an array of records', $name));
    }
    return $value;
}
```

Also, parseOffPeak with the `off_peak === null` check: the import needs to distinguish between "key absent (no change)" and "null (clear the value)". parseOffPeak returns null in both cases — the importer needs to know which one. On the importer side, we'll check `array_key_exists('off_peak', $raw)`. parseOffPeak is fine as-is.

Also, should I remove the unused ProviderSpec/ModelSpec in the psalm docblock? It's minor, so let's simplify the docblock.

